      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Let me add something to this post:\n\nGenerally, a modern GPU can render many triangles. They are often limited by VRAM. And there are quite players around with 8GB VRAM due prizes raises lately, they're not able to buy 12 or 16GB VRAM cards.\n\nTextures fills faster VRAM up. Triangles not really fast.\n\nTechnically, 5060Ti with 8 VRAM can still draw many triangles as 5060Ti 16GB version. But not for many textures, that will lead to freezes and frame drops, so 8GB version struggle earlier than 16GB version.\n\nSo yeah, i agreed triangles should not the main reason for ranking. It's often textures that fill up VRAM memory. This need more explained why its still 70,000 polygons. Many booth avatars are more than 70k btw, so all are already very poor labeled. But many are below 100k triangles.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
