      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c87baa8e6d1a57be67871ec|full_name}\n\n> This need more explained why its still 70,000 polygons.\n\n70,000 × 80 players = 5,600,000 triangles, and it's on the limit of what CPUs/GPUs can handle for skinned meshes (an RTX 5090 / 9800X3D setup doesn't achieve > 90 FPS in this scenario) - not static triangles -, and then there's people who put on \"just a little bit over the limit :)\" so you actually end up with more than 5,600,000 triangles and you have to account for the world that needs to be rendered and there's multiple passes with realtime lights and outlines.\n\nMoving the goalpost, making it even harder for the GTX 970 crowd (lowest supported minimum spec) to run VRChat. According to tupper on the Apr 10, 2026 developer stream, since 2020 the average performance hasn't improved with avatars, but decreased.\n\nThere's a secondary effect that happens when Unity Engine has to switch to a 32-bit mesh index buffer after 65,535 vertices in a mesh, but that's not a big deal.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
